<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank's Krupp says wants punctual euro launch.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank's Krupp says wants punctual euro launch.</headline>
<dateline>DORTMUND, Germany 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Krupp said on Saturday that it was crucial for Europe's single currency project to start on time in order to avoid disturbance on financial markets.</p>
<p>&quot;The potential for exchange rate disruption must be countered by a punctual realisation of currency union,&quot; Krupp told a meeting of the German opposition party, the Social Democrats (SPD).</p>
<p>Krupp added that this remained the case even if some European Union countries were not in a position to take part in Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) at the start, which is planned for January 1 1999.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
